1324
00:53:23.160 --> 00:53:27.720
Well, I worked in Canada for a bit, you know, and I have had these ketchup chips.
嗯，我在加拿大工作过一段时间，你知道的，我吃过这种番茄酱薯片。

1325
00:53:27.840 --> 00:53:28.740
Jenna, they're so good.
珍娜，它们太好吃了。

1326
00:53:29.060 --> 00:53:30.640
Listen to how they're described on the internet.
听听网上是怎么描述它们的。

1327
00:53:31.000 --> 00:53:36.360
They are the perfect balance of a delightful old Dutch chip layered with that lovely ketchup
它们是美味的荷兰老牌薯片与你渴望的那种可爱番茄酱味的完美平衡。

1328
00:53:36.360 --> 00:53:37.740
flavor you desire.
你渴望的味道。

1329
00:53:38.160 --> 00:53:41.480
But I don't desire a ketchup flavor on my potato chips.
但我并不渴望薯片上有番茄酱味。

1330
00:53:41.480 --> 00:53:43.040
Well, it might change your mind.
嗯，它可能会改变你的想法。

1331
00:53:43.040 --> 00:53:43.980
I'm just telling you.
我只是告诉你。

1332
00:53:44.120 --> 00:53:45.040
Maybe I will.
也许我会试试。

1333
00:53:45.780 --> 00:53:46.520
Chip people.
薯片达人。

1334
00:53:46.760 --> 00:53:48.040
Old Dutch chip people.
荷兰老牌薯片达人。

1335
00:53:48.140 --> 00:53:49.520
Will you send me a ketchup chip?
你能给我寄一包番茄酱薯片吗？

1336
00:53:49.640 --> 00:53:50.360
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1337
00:53:50.460 --> 00:53:50.980
Get ready.
准备好吧。

1338
00:53:51.560 --> 00:53:53.820
But listen, make sure some come my way.
但听着，一定要确保给我留点。

1339
00:53:54.080 --> 00:53:54.760
You got it.
没问题。

1340
00:53:54.880 --> 00:53:55.620
They're tangy.
它们酸酸甜甜的。

1341
00:53:55.680 --> 00:53:56.280
They're delicious.
它们很美味。

1342
00:53:56.960 --> 00:53:57.260
Okay.
好吧。

1343
00:53:57.880 --> 00:53:59.720
Guess who else is at the bar?
猜猜还有谁在吧台？

1344
00:54:00.440 --> 00:54:01.280
Concierge Marie.
礼宾员玛丽。

1345
00:54:01.780 --> 00:54:02.080
Yeah.
是啊。

1346
00:54:02.480 --> 00:54:05.920
Michael is, how you say, so excited to see her.
迈克尔怎么说呢，见到她非常兴奋。

1347
00:54:06.160 --> 00:54:06.440
Yeah.
是啊。

1348
00:54:06.960 --> 00:54:08.100
How do you say it?
你怎么说来着？

1349
00:54:08.340 --> 00:54:09.120
How do you say it?
你怎么说来着？

1350
00:54:09.600 --> 00:54:12.100
Andy's going to bring him two glasses of wine.
安迪要给他拿两杯红酒。

1351
00:54:12.480 --> 00:54:12.780
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1352
00:54:12.940 --> 00:54:14.240
He's going to get things started.
他准备要开始行动了。

1353
00:54:14.500 --> 00:54:14.700
Yeah.
没错。

1354
00:54:14.900 --> 00:54:19.200
He's also going to try to get things started for Oscar and a couple of gentlemen sitting
他还打算帮奥斯卡和坐在附近桌边的几位男士

1355
00:54:19.200 --> 00:54:20.240
at a table nearby.
也点上酒。

1356
00:54:20.560 --> 00:54:20.920
That's right.
没错。

1357
00:54:20.980 --> 00:54:26.900
He says to the bartender, Mademoiselle, beer me, dose Long Island iced teas, see vous play.
他对酒保说：小姐，给我来两杯长岛冰茶，拜托了。

1358
00:54:27.320 --> 00:54:28.840
Bad decision in a glass.
简直是杯装的错误决定。

1359
00:54:28.840 --> 00:54:30.880
It is a bad decision in a glass.
确实是杯装的错误决定。

1360
00:54:31.080 --> 00:54:31.940
It is a horrible decision.
那真是个糟糕的决定。

1361
00:54:32.140 --> 00:54:34.720
You know how you've had a volcano and you did the splits?
你知道你喝过火山鸡尾酒然后劈叉的事吗？

1362
00:54:34.980 --> 00:54:35.320
Yes.
知道。

1363
00:54:35.460 --> 00:54:37.360
I had some Long Island iced teas.
我喝过一些长岛冰茶。

1364
00:54:37.760 --> 00:54:38.280
Where?
在哪喝的？

1365
00:54:38.600 --> 00:54:42.100
In the Bahamas on spring break with my friends.
在巴哈马，和朋友们过春假的时候。

1366
00:54:42.660 --> 00:54:44.540
I never had one before.
我以前从没喝过。

1367
00:54:44.920 --> 00:54:48.800
I wasn't 21 yet, but in the Bahamas, you can drink when you're 18.
我当时还没满21岁，但在巴哈马，18岁就可以喝酒了。

1368
00:54:49.260 --> 00:54:55.060
We went to the casino and they just give them to you free if you sit at the slot machines.
我们去了赌场，只要坐在老虎机前，他们就会免费给你提供。

1369
00:54:55.340 --> 00:54:55.940
I have not.
我没喝过。

1370
00:54:55.940 --> 00:54:58.300
All of this was like, what is happening?
当时我整个人都懵了，心想这是怎么回事？

1371
00:54:58.300 --> 00:55:00.480
I have not had a Long Island iced tea.
我没喝过长岛冰茶。

1372
00:55:00.660 --> 00:55:02.780
I've had the volcano, but it's just the same thing.
我喝过火山鸡尾酒，但其实都一样。

1373
00:55:02.840 --> 00:55:04.560
They just dump a bunch of booze in it, right?
他们就是往里面倒了一堆酒，对吧？

1374
00:55:04.620 --> 00:55:06.480
It's like seven or eight different liquors.
里面大概混了七八种不同的烈酒。

1375
00:55:07.480 --> 00:55:07.920
Tasty.
味道不错。

1376
00:55:08.120 --> 00:55:09.220
Went down easy.
喝起来很顺口。

1377
00:55:09.480 --> 00:55:09.980
Well, yeah.
嗯，确实。

1378
00:55:10.460 --> 00:55:11.540
Then a lot of vomiting.
然后就是一阵狂吐。

1379
00:55:11.740 --> 00:55:12.940
A lot of vomiting.
吐得一塌糊涂。

1380
00:55:13.300 --> 00:55:16.980
Well, we got a fan question about this scene from Evan L.
好吧，我们收到一个粉丝关于这一幕的提问，来自Evan L。

1381
00:55:17.500 --> 00:55:23.100
At 11 minutes, 14 seconds, Andy says, you will thank me when they spank thee.
在11分14秒时，安迪说：当你被拍屁股时，你会感谢我的。

1382
00:55:23.500 --> 00:55:26.100
And he wants to know who came up with that line.
他想知道这句台词是谁想出来的。

1383
00:55:26.480 --> 00:55:27.300
Can I guess?
我能猜猜吗？

1384
00:55:27.300 --> 00:55:27.900
Sure.
当然。

1385
00:55:28.340 --> 00:55:28.900
Lee or Jean?
是李还是吉恩？

1386
00:55:30.440 --> 00:55:31.740
That's a good guess.
猜得不错。

1387
00:55:32.200 --> 00:55:33.500
It's in the script.
那是剧本里写的。

1388
00:55:33.500 --> 00:55:35.540
And I asked Brent Forrester about it.
我问过布伦特·福雷斯特关于这件事。

1389
00:55:35.640 --> 00:55:40.940
And he said he is the author of the thank me spank thee line.
他说那句“感谢我，拍屁股”的台词是他写的。

1390
00:55:40.940 --> 00:55:47.660
He said there are few things more fun than writing a rhyming punchline for the Andy character.
他说没什么比给安迪这个角色写押韵的俏皮话更有趣的了。

1391
00:55:47.980 --> 00:55:53.820
He said he got a little bit too into writing rhyming punchlines for Ed that season.
他说那一季他给艾德写押韵俏皮话写得有点过头了。

1392
00:55:54.040 --> 00:56:00.120
He said that one day in the writer's room, he pitched a line where Andy refers to his quote,
他说有一天在编剧室里，他提议了一句台词，安迪引用了他的话：

1393
00:56:00.120 --> 00:56:02.480
back up, snack pack, backpack.
退后，零食包，背包。

1394
00:56:03.660 --> 00:56:09.960
And he said at that point, the writers forbid him from writing any more rhyming punchlines for the rest of the year.
他说从那以后，编剧们就禁止他在那一年剩下的时间里再写任何押韵的俏皮话了。

1395
00:56:09.960 --> 00:56:12.440
I wonder if he wrote Nifty Gifties.
不知道“俏皮礼物”是不是他写的。

1396
00:56:12.920 --> 00:56:14.080
He might have.
可能是他写的。

1397
00:56:14.220 --> 00:56:15.500
Oh, Brent, that's so good.
噢，布伦特，那太棒了。

1398
00:56:16.760 --> 00:56:18.100
Well, guess what?
好吧，你猜怎么着？

1399
00:56:18.560 --> 00:56:20.280
They're not going to spank him.
他们才不会拍他屁股呢。

1400
00:56:20.560 --> 00:56:21.120
They're not.
确实不会。

1401
00:56:21.400 --> 00:56:22.320
They turn him down.
他们拒绝了他。

1402
00:56:22.320 --> 00:56:27.180
And Oscar and Andy now drink the Long Island iced teas, which is going to lead to some trouble.
奥斯卡和安迪现在喝起了长岛冰茶，这要惹出麻烦了。

1403
00:56:27.460 --> 00:56:33.440
Some real trouble because Oscar says to Andy, what do you see in Angela?
真的麻烦，因为奥斯卡问安迪，你到底看上安吉拉哪一点？

1404
00:56:33.820 --> 00:56:36.060
And again, I was hungry as I watched this.
再说一次，我看着这一幕的时候饿了。

1405
00:56:36.300 --> 00:56:43.800
So at 12 minutes, 17 seconds, I can see another bag of old Dutch potato chips sitting next to Oscar's arm on the bar.
所以在12分17秒的时候，我能看到奥斯卡手臂旁边的吧台上放着另一袋老荷兰薯片。

1406
00:56:43.960 --> 00:56:45.280
They're the green and white bag.
那是绿白相间的袋子。

1407
00:56:45.380 --> 00:56:46.180
You know what that means.
你知道那意味着什么吗？

1408
00:56:46.420 --> 00:56:47.360
Sour cream and onion?
酸奶油洋葱味？

1409
00:56:47.680 --> 00:56:49.280
They are the dill pickle chips.
那是莳萝泡菜味的薯片。

1410
00:56:49.820 --> 00:56:50.080
What?
什么？

1411
00:56:50.720 --> 00:56:51.120
Yep.
没错。

1412
00:56:51.880 --> 00:56:52.820
Described on the Internet.
网上有介绍。

1413
00:56:53.160 --> 00:56:54.520
Do they make any regular flavors?
他们做普通口味的吗？

1414
00:56:55.120 --> 00:56:55.820
They do.
做的。

1415
00:56:56.040 --> 00:56:58.020
I'm telling you, these chips are so good.
我跟你说，这些薯片太好吃了。

1416
00:56:58.260 --> 00:57:00.000
You've had the dill pickle ones?
你吃过莳萝泡菜味的？

1417
00:57:00.060 --> 00:57:01.140
I have sampled.
我尝过。

1418
00:57:01.400 --> 00:57:04.460
You know, like on set, we would have a whole bunch of bags of chips.
你知道，在片场，我们会有好几袋薯片。

1419
00:57:05.780 --> 00:57:07.380
They're real salty, and I liked it.
它们真的很咸，我喜欢。

1420
00:57:07.380 --> 00:57:09.280
I guess I'm a chip traditionaliSt.
我想我是一个薯片传统主义者。

1421
00:57:09.560 --> 00:57:10.100
You know what?
你知道吗？

1422
00:57:10.140 --> 00:57:11.360
You need to be a chip traveler.
你需要成为一个薯片旅行者。

1423
00:57:11.680 --> 00:57:12.200
All right.
好吧。

1424
00:57:12.420 --> 00:57:14.480
You need to try some international chips.
你需要尝试一些国际口味的薯片。

1425
00:57:14.760 --> 00:57:15.440
I'll try them.
我会试试的。

1426
00:57:15.620 --> 00:57:17.140
Well, the dill ones are real salty.
嗯，莳萝味的真的很咸。

1427
00:57:18.560 --> 00:57:19.800
I do like a pickle.
我确实喜欢泡菜。

1428
00:57:20.080 --> 00:57:20.600
I know.
我知道。

1429
00:57:21.240 --> 00:57:25.540
But anyway, Andy drunk dials Angela.
但不管怎样，安迪醉醺醺地给安吉拉打了电话。

1430
00:57:25.800 --> 00:57:27.660
This is a huge mistake.
这是一个巨大的错误。

1431
00:57:27.860 --> 00:57:28.640
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

1432
00:57:28.660 --> 00:57:29.700
He says, you know what?
他说，你知道吗？

1433
00:57:29.780 --> 00:57:30.880
We're going to discuss this.
我们要讨论一下这件事。

1434
00:57:31.000 --> 00:57:32.700
We will discuss this naked.
我们要赤身裸体地讨论这件事。

1435
00:57:33.020 --> 00:57:35.460
But then there's a voice in the background.
但背景里有个声音。

1436
00:57:36.260 --> 00:57:38.240
I mean, she's with Dwight.
我是说，她和德怀特在一起。

1437
00:57:38.460 --> 00:57:39.600
Of course she is.
当然是这样。

1438
00:57:39.840 --> 00:57:40.260
Yeah.
是啊。

1439
00:57:40.500 --> 00:57:44.580
But somehow Andy doesn't totally register it.
但不知何故，安迪并没有完全意识到这一点。

1440
00:57:44.580 --> 00:57:46.300
He's had a Long Island iced tea.
他喝了一杯长岛冰茶。

1441
00:57:46.640 --> 00:57:47.920
Several, I think, at this point.
我想此时已经喝了好几杯了。

1442
00:57:48.660 --> 00:57:49.980
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

1443
00:57:50.120 --> 00:57:52.520
Michael and Concierge Marie, they're clicking.
迈克尔和礼宾员玛丽，他们很合得来。

1444
00:57:52.880 --> 00:57:53.980
They're going to leave.
他们要离开了。

1445
00:57:53.980 --> 00:57:56.900
They're going to smooch outside in the alley.
他们要去外面的小巷里亲热。

1446
00:57:57.100 --> 00:58:00.860
And we asked Wendy about this, about kissing Steve.
我们问过温迪关于这件事，关于亲吻史蒂夫。

1447
00:58:01.060 --> 00:58:02.240
And here's what she had to say.
这是她要说的。

1448
00:58:02.240 --> 00:58:07.360
I was super nervous to kiss Steve Carell.
亲吻史蒂夫·卡瑞尔让我超级紧张。

1449
00:58:07.620 --> 00:58:13.260
I was so nervous that I was practically going into convulsions.
我紧张得几乎要抽搐了。

1450
00:58:14.020 --> 00:58:17.940
But I did it, and it was great, and I highly recommend it.
但我还是做了，感觉很棒，我强烈推荐。

1451
00:58:19.840 --> 00:58:21.420
She highly recommends.
她极力推荐。

1452
00:58:21.720 --> 00:58:22.260
Oh, well.
噢，好吧。

1453
00:58:22.480 --> 00:58:24.780
They're not just going to kiss outside the hotel.
他们可不只是在酒店外亲吻而已。

1454
00:58:25.020 --> 00:58:25.680
All right?
好吗？

1455
00:58:25.820 --> 00:58:30.780
We are going to cut to Michael being sort of shoved out of her.
我们要剪辑一段迈克尔被她赶出来的画面。

1456
00:58:30.980 --> 00:58:32.340
Room 887.
887号房。

1457
00:58:32.880 --> 00:58:33.180
Yeah.
是啊。

1458
00:58:33.540 --> 00:58:34.720
Without his shoes.
没穿鞋。

1459
00:58:34.960 --> 00:58:35.400
Barefoot.
光着脚。

1460
00:58:35.520 --> 00:58:36.800
He's shuffling down the hall.
他正拖着步子走在走廊里。

1461
00:58:37.120 --> 00:58:37.600
I know.
我知道。

1462
00:58:37.600 --> 00:58:39.560
And then she's like, wait, you forgot your shoes.
然后她就像是说，等等，你忘了你的鞋子。

1463
00:58:39.560 --> 00:58:40.540
Only she says nothing.
只是她什么也没说。

1464
00:58:40.780 --> 00:58:43.200
She just sets them out and quickly shuts the door.
她只是把鞋放出来，然后迅速关上了门。

1465
00:58:43.960 --> 00:58:46.760
Well, that kind of wraps up Concierge Marie.
好吧，礼宾员玛丽的故事就到此为止了。

1466
00:58:47.260 --> 00:58:52.520
We had to ask Wendy if she ever gets recognized for being on the show.
我们不得不问温迪，她是否因为出演这部剧而被认出来过。

1467
00:58:52.580 --> 00:58:53.660
And here's what she said.
以下是她的回答。

1468
00:58:54.120 --> 00:58:54.600
Yes.
是的。

1469
00:58:55.180 --> 00:58:56.360
So many times.
很多次。

1470
00:58:56.360 --> 00:59:00.620
I'm so surprised at that because I was, you know, barely in it.
我对此感到非常惊讶，因为你知道，我几乎没怎么出镜。

1471
00:59:00.720 --> 00:59:05.280
But, you know, that just speaks to the reach and the popularity of the office.
但你知道，这恰恰说明了《办公室》的影响力和受欢迎程度。

1472
00:59:05.900 --> 00:59:07.760
I read a fun fact about Wendy.
我读到过一个关于温迪的趣事。

1473
00:59:08.140 --> 00:59:08.900
Yes, you did.
没错，你读到过。

1474
00:59:09.040 --> 00:59:09.500
Share it, Jenna.
分享一下吧，珍娜。

1475
00:59:09.640 --> 00:59:10.200
It's so good.
太棒了。

1476
00:59:10.420 --> 00:59:10.680
Okay.
好的。

1477
00:59:11.100 --> 00:59:18.600
Wendy was the editor for California State University's Academic Journal of Social Work.
温迪曾是加州州立大学《社会工作学术期刊》的编辑。

1478
00:59:18.800 --> 00:59:21.860
This was her day job before she hit it big as an actress.
这是她在作为演员成名之前的主业。

1479
00:59:22.100 --> 00:59:29.100
But even after she was working all the time, she kept her job until 2012.
但即使在工作邀约不断之后，她还是保留了这份工作直到2012年。

1480
00:59:30.140 --> 00:59:32.440
Bridesmaids came out in 2011.
《伴娘》是在2011年上映的。

1481
00:59:32.440 --> 00:59:37.600
So even after Bridesmaids, she was still editing this journal of social work.
所以即使在《伴娘》之后，她依然在编辑这本社会工作期刊。

1482
00:59:37.600 --> 00:59:39.540
And we had to ask her about it.
我们必须问问她这件事。

1483
00:59:39.740 --> 00:59:40.680
Here's what she said.
以下是她的回答。

1484
00:59:40.840 --> 00:59:47.560
It is true that while I was building my acting career and, you know, doing pretty well,
确实，当我在发展演艺事业并且，你知道，做得还不错的时候，

1485
00:59:47.720 --> 00:59:51.020
that I kept my side job at Cal State Long Beach.
我保留了我在加州州立大学长滩分校的副业。

1486
00:59:51.280 --> 00:59:55.660
I was an assistant editor for a social work journal.
我曾是一家社会工作期刊的助理编辑。

1487
00:59:55.660 --> 01:00:01.660
I did that for 12 years, all through Reno 911, all through, you know, all these movies that
我做了12年，贯穿了整个《雷诺911》，贯穿了，你知道，我拍的所有这些电影，

1488
01:00:01.660 --> 01:00:05.740
I did, Rules of Engagement, and right up until the Goldbergs.
《约会规则》，一直到《戈德堡一家》之前。

1489
01:00:05.980 --> 01:00:10.520
And the only reason I'm not doing it anymore is because the journal folded.
我不再做这份工作的唯一原因就是期刊停刊了。

1490
01:00:10.580 --> 01:00:12.040
It went out of business.
它倒闭了。

1491
01:00:12.740 --> 01:00:14.680
But it was a great job.
但那是一份很棒的工作。

1492
01:00:14.680 --> 01:00:17.340
It was like not even 20 hours a week.
每周工作时间甚至不到20小时。

1493
01:00:17.340 --> 01:00:19.520
I could do it from wherever I was.
无论我在哪里都能做。

1494
01:00:19.520 --> 01:00:23.220
And it was all about, you know, people in the social work profession.
而且内容全是关于，你知道，社会工作专业人士的。

1495
01:00:23.500 --> 01:00:27.840
And let's be honest, those people deserve a lot of credit for what they do.
说实话，这些人所做的工作值得极大的赞誉。

1496
01:00:28.000 --> 01:00:29.260
They don't get recognized enough.
他们得到的认可还不够多。

1497
01:00:29.660 --> 01:00:30.640
Yeah, it was great.
是啊，那真的很棒。

1498
01:00:30.640 --> 01:00:32.160
And I loved doing it.
我热爱这份工作。

1499
01:00:32.260 --> 01:00:37.540
I loved my original boss who used to come and see my shows at the Groundlings.
我喜欢我最初的老板，她过去常来看我在“地堡剧团”的演出。

1500
01:00:37.680 --> 01:00:41.620
Like she was just so super supportive that she said, please don't ever quit.
她真的非常支持我，甚至说，请千万别辞职。

1501
01:00:41.860 --> 01:00:45.480
So I kept my word and I stayed until the very end.
所以我信守承诺，一直待到了最后。

1502
01:00:45.480 --> 01:00:48.460
See what I was saying about amazing human being?
看吧，我刚才说什么来着，她真是个了不起的人，对吧？

1503
01:00:48.740 --> 01:00:49.600
I love her.
我爱她。

1504
01:00:49.880 --> 01:00:52.100
You know, that was so moving to me when I heard it.
你知道吗，我听到那番话时真的很感动。

1505
01:00:52.320 --> 01:00:53.920
My niece is a social worker.
我的侄女就是一名社会工作者。

1506
01:00:54.840 --> 01:01:00.180
I'm just always, you know, honestly, guys, I'm lifting her up in prayer all the time because
老实说，伙计们，我一直都在为她祈祷，因为

1507
01:01:00.760 --> 01:01:02.180
it's not an easy job.
这份工作并不轻松。

1508
01:01:02.180 --> 01:01:06.500
And I'm thankful that we have people that have a passion for helping others in that way.
我很庆幸有这样一群人，他们热衷于以这种方式帮助他人。

1509
01:01:06.820 --> 01:01:12.100
Yeah, it's not an easy job because sometimes you have to see and confront real hard things.
没错，这确实不容易，因为有时你必须直面那些非常残酷的现实。

1510
01:01:12.340 --> 01:01:12.500
Yes.
是的。

1511
01:01:12.880 --> 01:01:14.620
And then you have to hold that.
而且你还得承受这一切。

1512
01:01:14.860 --> 01:01:15.160
Yeah.
没错。

1513
01:01:15.480 --> 01:01:16.020
Yeah.
是啊。

1514
01:01:16.500 --> 01:01:22.120
Well, as if you needed another reason to love Wendy, I would also like to share that
好吧，如果说你还需要另一个爱温迪的理由，我想分享的是

1515
01:01:22.120 --> 01:01:30.840
in 2009, 2010, and 2011, she rang in the new year performing at military bases in Iraq
在2009年、2010年和2011年，她都在伊拉克和科威特的军事基地

1516
01:01:30.840 --> 01:01:31.640
and Kuwait.
演出，迎接新年。

1517
01:01:31.940 --> 01:01:36.400
And she went to the smaller bases that a lot of people didn't go to that kind of rarely
她去了很多很少有人去的小型基地，那些地方几乎

1518
01:01:36.400 --> 01:01:37.140
get entertainment.
没什么娱乐活动。

1519
01:01:37.560 --> 01:01:38.380
Love that.
太棒了。

1520
01:01:38.560 --> 01:01:39.220
Love you.
爱你。

1521
01:01:39.380 --> 01:01:41.460
Wendy, thank you so much.
温迪，非常感谢你。

1522
01:01:41.560 --> 01:01:43.160
It was so great to reconnect with you.
能和你重新取得联系真是太好了。

1523
01:01:43.320 --> 01:01:45.320
Thanks for sharing your memories of the office.
感谢你分享关于《办公室》的回忆。

1524
01:01:45.480 --> 01:01:48.380
You guys, you can find Wendy in so many places.
各位，你们可以在很多地方找到温迪。

1525
01:01:48.380 --> 01:01:49.400
She's so talented.
她非常有才华。

1526
01:01:49.660 --> 01:01:52.320
She has a podcast called Generation Ripe.
她有一个播客叫《Generation Ripe》。

1527
01:01:52.540 --> 01:01:54.900
It is for teenagers over 40.
那是为40岁以上的“青少年”准备的。

1528
01:01:55.500 --> 01:02:00.640
It's described as a Generation Ripe listener is someone who thinks of their age as an asset,
对《Generation Ripe》听众的定义是：那些将年龄视为资产

1529
01:02:00.800 --> 01:02:01.680
not a liability.
而非负担的人。

1530
01:02:02.020 --> 01:02:05.840
We are older people with young souls are younger people with old souls.
我们是拥有年轻灵魂的老年人，或是拥有老灵魂的年轻人。

1531
01:02:05.840 --> 01:02:08.260
Of course, she's on the Goldbergs.
当然，她还出演了《戈德堡一家》。

1532
01:02:08.340 --> 01:02:09.740
They're about to start season nine.
他们马上就要开始第九季了。

1533
01:02:10.040 --> 01:02:15.380
She's on a Marvel series on Hulu called Modak and just tons of other things, you guys.
她还在Hulu的漫威剧集《魔多客》里有演出，还有其他很多作品，伙计们。

1534
01:02:15.540 --> 01:02:19.780
And you can find her on Instagram at Wendy McClendon Covey.
你们可以在Instagram上关注她，账号是Wendy McClendon Covey。

1535
01:02:19.780 --> 01:02:20.440
Yes.
没错。

1536
01:02:20.760 --> 01:02:21.540
Let's see.
让我们看看。

1537
01:02:21.660 --> 01:02:22.680
Where should we go?
我们该去哪儿呢？

1538
01:02:22.680 --> 01:02:24.320
It's the next day.
已经是第二天了。

1539
01:02:24.880 --> 01:02:26.440
Oh, people are hungover.
哦，大家都有宿醉。

1540
01:02:26.620 --> 01:02:27.900
Very hungover.
宿醉很严重。

1541
01:02:28.360 --> 01:02:31.520
Andy does not remember calling Angela.
安迪不记得给安吉拉打过电话了。

1542
01:02:31.840 --> 01:02:32.740
I know.
我知道。

1543
01:02:33.140 --> 01:02:33.880
Oh, no.
哦，不。

1544
01:02:34.660 --> 01:02:35.200
Oh.
哦。

1545
01:02:35.200 --> 01:02:38.040
Michael is very melancholy.
迈克尔非常忧郁。

1546
01:02:38.220 --> 01:02:38.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1547
01:02:38.680 --> 01:02:44.260
And he has to go sell paper at Catalyst Paper, which I looked it up.
他得去Catalyst Paper卖纸，我查过了。

1548
01:02:44.440 --> 01:02:44.640
Yeah.
没错。

1549
01:02:45.100 --> 01:02:51.500
It's a real Canadian paper company, but it looks like its headquarters is based in Richmond,
那是一家真实的加拿大造纸公司，但看起来总部设在

1550
01:02:51.740 --> 01:02:54.520
British Columbia, which is over on the West CoaSt.
不列颠哥伦比亚省的列治文，就在西海岸那边。

1551
01:02:54.800 --> 01:02:57.340
I could not find a Winnipeg branch.
我没能找到温尼伯分部。

1552
01:02:57.700 --> 01:03:00.000
I mean, if you couldn't, I doubt it's there.
我的意思是，如果你都找不到，那它肯定不在那儿。

1553
01:03:00.500 --> 01:03:04.540
David Wallace calls to congratulate Michael because he did it.
大卫·华莱士打电话来祝贺迈克尔，因为他成功了。

1554
01:03:04.540 --> 01:03:05.660
He got the sale.
他谈成了这笔生意。

1555
01:03:06.340 --> 01:03:07.740
Michael is mad.
迈克尔很生气。

1556
01:03:08.000 --> 01:03:13.000
Yeah, because he's realized that this trip was a Band-Aid to try to help his feelings
是啊，因为他意识到这次出差只是为了安抚他对于

1557
01:03:13.000 --> 01:03:14.420
about Holly being transferred.
霍莉被调走而产生的失落感。

1558
01:03:14.740 --> 01:03:15.640
He's upset.
他很难过。

1559
01:03:15.840 --> 01:03:17.320
And he tells him off.
于是他把对方臭骂了一顿。

1560
01:03:17.420 --> 01:03:17.700
Yeah.
没错。

1561
01:03:17.940 --> 01:03:19.620
I have a location breakdown.
我有一份外景地明细。

1562
01:03:20.520 --> 01:03:21.920
Why do you say it like that?
你为什么要那样说？

1563
01:03:22.260 --> 01:03:22.920
I don't know.
我不知道。

1564
01:03:23.160 --> 01:03:24.100
You said it like sad sack.
你刚才说得像个丧气鬼一样。

1565
01:03:24.320 --> 01:03:25.320
You said it like this.
你是这样说的。

1566
01:03:25.440 --> 01:03:27.100
I have a location breakdown.
我有一份外景地明细。

1567
01:03:27.100 --> 01:03:28.760
Well, I'm sad with Michael.
好吧，我是在为迈克尔感到难过。

1568
01:03:28.980 --> 01:03:29.340
Aw.
噢。

1569
01:03:29.740 --> 01:03:29.960
Yeah.
是啊。

1570
01:03:29.960 --> 01:03:34.640
For the Winnipeg Airport for these scenes, we used Terminal No.
为了拍摄这些温尼伯机场的戏份，我们使用了洛杉矶国际机场的2号航站楼。

1571
01:03:34.780 --> 01:03:36.420
2 at LAX.
2号航站楼。

1572
01:03:36.780 --> 01:03:42.460
Randy let me know that there was an area that was out of service at that time and that our
兰迪告诉我当时那里有一个区域处于停用状态，我们的

1573
01:03:42.460 --> 01:03:48.260
location manager, Kyle Alexander, was able to get an agreement from the LAX airport to
外景经理凯尔·亚历山大成功与洛杉矶机场达成协议，

1574
01:03:48.260 --> 01:03:49.080
let us film there.
让我们在那里拍摄。

1575
01:03:49.280 --> 01:03:50.520
That's like unheard of.
这简直是闻所未闻。

1576
01:03:50.700 --> 01:03:51.140
Well...
嗯……

1577
01:03:51.140 --> 01:03:52.760
LAX does not let you film.
洛杉矶机场通常是不让拍摄的。

1578
01:03:52.940 --> 01:03:53.740
Like, they are hardcore.
他们管得非常严。

1579
01:03:53.740 --> 01:03:59.180
Well, especially after 9-11, they had incredibly strict airport security.
尤其是9·11事件之后，他们的机场安保极其严格。

1580
01:03:59.800 --> 01:04:05.480
So we were only allowed a very small number of cast and crew and extras.
所以我们只被允许带极少数的演职人员和群演进入。

1581
01:04:05.860 --> 01:04:11.340
Everybody had to submit credentials very far in advance and had to be screened.
每个人都必须提前很久提交证件并接受审查。

1582
01:04:11.460 --> 01:04:15.380
So he said they had to create what they called a micro unit.
所以他说他们必须组建一个所谓的“微型摄制组”。

1583
01:04:15.920 --> 01:04:17.480
That's how small it was.
规模就是这么小。

1584
01:04:17.660 --> 01:04:23.140
He said that the airplanes outside the window were not Air Canada planes.
他说窗外的飞机并不是加拿大航空的飞机。

1585
01:04:23.700 --> 01:04:29.960
They had to paint over the logos using visual effects during post-production.
他们必须在后期制作中通过视觉特效把标志覆盖掉。

1586
01:04:29.960 --> 01:04:33.780
And so they put the red maple leaf on the tail of one of the planes.
于是他们在其中一架飞机的尾部加上了红枫叶标志。

1587
01:04:34.360 --> 01:04:36.380
We could only afford to do one plane.
我们只负担得起处理一架飞机。

1588
01:04:36.780 --> 01:04:39.520
If you look over Michael's shoulder, it's on the left.
如果你看向迈克尔的肩膀那边，它就在左侧。

1589
01:04:39.660 --> 01:04:40.460
Yeah, I saw it.
嗯，我看到了。

1590
01:04:41.260 --> 01:04:46.660
Well, before we get to this big business with Jim and Pam, we should probably let you know
好吧，在进入吉姆和帕姆的重头戏之前，我们应该先告诉你，

1591
01:04:46.660 --> 01:04:49.620
that Kelly is going to break up with Daryl.
凯莉打算和达里尔分手。

1592
01:04:49.980 --> 01:04:52.160
I mean, Ryan has a text ready to go.
我是说，瑞安已经写好了短信准备发送。

1593
01:04:52.160 --> 01:04:53.780
They just have to hit send together.
他们只需要一起按下发送键就行了。

1594
01:04:54.280 --> 01:04:56.460
And I think, what does Ryan want?
我在想，瑞安到底想要什么？

1595
01:04:56.600 --> 01:04:59.180
Does he want Daryl to come upstairs and make a scene?
他是想让达里尔冲上楼来大闹一场吗？

1596
01:04:59.360 --> 01:05:00.420
What does Ryan want?
瑞安到底想要什么？

1597
01:05:00.560 --> 01:05:02.820
He wants to be the other guy.
他想当那个“第三者”。

1598
01:05:03.480 --> 01:05:03.660
Yeah.
没错。

1599
01:05:03.800 --> 01:05:06.080
He wants a reaction out of Daryl.
他想看到达里尔的反应。

1600
01:05:06.500 --> 01:05:08.140
Daryl seems relieved.
达里尔看起来如释重负。

1601
01:05:08.280 --> 01:05:10.660
He's whistling as he walks to his car.
他一边吹着口哨，一边走向自己的车。

1602
01:05:10.780 --> 01:05:11.860
He responds immediately.
他立刻回应了。

1603
01:05:11.860 --> 01:05:12.600
Okay, cool.
好的，酷。

1604
01:05:12.820 --> 01:05:16.000
And then literally is like doing a dance to his pickup truck.
然后他简直就像是在跳着舞走向他的皮卡车。

1605
01:05:16.180 --> 01:05:16.400
Yeah.
是啊。

1606
01:05:16.400 --> 01:05:19.120
He's like, whew, thank you, Ryan.
他就像是在说，呼，谢谢你，瑞安。

1607
01:05:19.500 --> 01:05:24.600
And that then, of course, immediately makes Ryan less interested in this relationship.
而这当然立刻让瑞安对这段关系没那么感兴趣了。

1608
01:05:24.860 --> 01:05:25.440
And here we go.
我们要开始了。

1609
01:05:25.560 --> 01:05:26.000
And they're back.
他们回来了。

1610
01:05:26.000 --> 01:05:26.520
Here we go.
开始了。

1611
01:05:27.320 --> 01:05:28.120
All right.
好吧。

1612
01:05:28.600 --> 01:05:30.040
Jim is going to leave.
吉姆要离开了。

1613
01:05:30.300 --> 01:05:32.800
And again, you guys have this Jim and Pam scene.
再说一次，你们这儿有一场吉姆和帕姆的戏。

1614
01:05:33.060 --> 01:05:36.980
At that golden hour, your hair is sparkling with sunshine.
在那个黄金时刻，你的头发在阳光下闪闪发光。

1615
01:05:37.440 --> 01:05:40.060
It's like that sunset scene in the parking lot.
就像停车场里的那个日落场景一样。

1616
01:05:40.160 --> 01:05:41.220
You couldn't look cuter.
你看起来可爱极了。

1617
01:05:41.420 --> 01:05:42.060
I know.
我知道。

1618
01:05:42.060 --> 01:05:44.300
I thought this scene was really sweet.
我觉得这场戏真的很甜。

1619
01:05:44.780 --> 01:05:45.260
Yeah.
是啊。

1620
01:05:45.500 --> 01:05:47.840
Pam is standing in the parking lot.
帕姆站在停车场里。

1621
01:05:48.000 --> 01:05:50.240
And Jim says, what are you doing here?
吉姆问她，你在这里做什么？

1622
01:05:50.600 --> 01:05:55.500
Because he had told her on the phone, when you come back, you're going to come back the right way.
因为他在电话里告诉过她，当你回来的时候，你要以正确的方式回来。

1623
01:05:55.760 --> 01:05:56.120
Right.
没错。

1624
01:05:56.200 --> 01:05:56.960
And he's supportive.
而且他很支持她。

1625
01:05:56.960 --> 01:05:59.680
If she wants to take the class again, they'll get through it.
如果她想重修这门课，他们会一起克服的。

1626
01:05:59.740 --> 01:06:00.000
Yes.
是的。

1627
01:06:00.100 --> 01:06:05.380
That the right way to come back is for her to come back having graduated from art school.
所谓正确的回归方式，就是让她从艺术学校毕业后再回来。

1628
01:06:05.980 --> 01:06:07.380
So Pam's standing there.
所以帕姆站在那里。

1629
01:06:07.380 --> 01:06:10.220
And she says, I'm coming back the wrong way.
她说，我以错误的方式回来了。

1630
01:06:10.220 --> 01:06:12.100
But she's okay with it.
但她对此并不介意。

1631
01:06:12.200 --> 01:06:13.360
She's happy about it.
她为此感到高兴。

1632
01:06:13.620 --> 01:06:14.640
She missed Scranton.
她想念斯克兰顿了。

1633
01:06:14.800 --> 01:06:15.560
She missed Jim.
她想念吉姆了。

1634
01:06:15.840 --> 01:06:19.300
She actually hated the graphic design school.
她其实讨厌那所平面设计学校。

1635
01:06:19.700 --> 01:06:20.200
Yeah.
是啊。

1636
01:06:20.460 --> 01:06:24.060
She tells Jim, this isn't really what I wanted to do.
她告诉吉姆，这并不是我真正想做的事。

1637
01:06:24.220 --> 01:06:26.100
But she had to go to find that out.
但她必须去尝试一下才能发现这一点。

1638
01:06:26.240 --> 01:06:26.820
She did.
她确实去了。

1639
01:06:27.140 --> 01:06:29.520
You know, we had a question from Evan L.
你知道，我们收到了埃文·L的一个问题。

1640
01:06:29.840 --> 01:06:33.180
Why did the writers have Pam fail art school?
为什么编剧要让帕姆在艺术学校失败？

1641
01:06:33.440 --> 01:06:34.960
Well, that's a good question, Evan.
嗯，这是个好问题，埃文。

1642
01:06:35.420 --> 01:06:37.420
I asked Brent Forrester about it.
我问过布伦特·福雷斯特关于这件事的情况。

1643
01:06:37.420 --> 01:06:45.460
He said that the story of Pam failing art school and coming back, quote, the wrong way was a pitch from Jen Salata.
他说帕姆在艺术学校失败并以“错误的方式”回来的故事，是简·萨拉塔提出的构思。

1644
01:06:46.000 --> 01:06:48.280
Brent said, I have a daughter.
布伦特说，我有一个女儿。

1645
01:06:48.420 --> 01:06:51.300
And he said, I'm a big fat feminiSt.
他说，我是一个彻头彻尾的女权主义者。

1646
01:06:51.300 --> 01:06:52.160
That's a quote.
这是他的原话。

1647
01:06:52.560 --> 01:06:58.460
And the idea that Pam would give up on her dreams to be with a man really rubbed him the wrong way.
帕姆为了和一个男人在一起而放弃梦想的想法，让他感到非常不舒服。

1648
01:06:58.460 --> 01:07:06.580
But that Jen Salata absolutely insisted that the romantic power of this gesture outweighed any politics.
但简·萨拉塔坚持认为，这种姿态所带来的浪漫力量胜过任何政治考量。

1649
01:07:07.040 --> 01:07:20.660
And also that the truth for Pam was not that she was giving up on her dreams for Jim, but that she was distinguishing what her real dreams were.
而且对帕姆来说，事实并非她为了吉姆放弃梦想，而是她在认清自己真正的梦想是什么。

1650
01:07:21.180 --> 01:07:32.300
And I really liked that because I think what Pam did here in going to graphic design school was that she was taking her real dream of being a creative artiSt.
我真的很喜欢这一点，因为我认为帕姆去读平面设计学校所做的事情，是她在追求自己成为一名创意艺术家的真正梦想。

1651
01:07:32.760 --> 01:07:35.180
And she was doing what a lot of artists do.
她当时在做很多艺术家都会做的事。

1652
01:07:35.280 --> 01:07:38.540
And she was trying to find a practical application.
她试图找到一种实际的应用方式。

1653
01:07:39.180 --> 01:07:39.300
Right.
没错。

1654
01:07:39.420 --> 01:07:41.380
How can I sort of do art but make a living?
我该怎么在搞艺术的同时又能维持生计呢？

1655
01:07:41.560 --> 01:07:41.880
Yeah.
是啊。

1656
01:07:42.020 --> 01:07:42.140
Right?
对吧？

1657
01:07:42.140 --> 01:07:43.640
Yes, exactly.
没错，正是如此。

1658
01:07:44.000 --> 01:07:49.840
But, you know, I mean, people go into graphic design when they're passionate about graphic design.
但你要知道，我是说，人们选择平面设计是因为他们热爱平面设计。

1659
01:07:49.880 --> 01:07:51.720
It's not some backup job.
那可不是什么备选工作。

1660
01:07:51.860 --> 01:07:51.980
Right?
对吧？

1661
01:07:52.280 --> 01:07:57.300
And the truth is, is that Pam discovered she does not have a passion for graphic design.
事实是，帕姆发现她对平面设计根本没有热情。

1662
01:07:57.360 --> 01:08:02.840
And that's sort of what I had in my head when I was doing that scene on the phone with Jim and Pam's crying.
我在拍那场吉姆和帕姆哭泣的电话戏时，脑子里想的就是这些。

1663
01:08:03.340 --> 01:08:08.120
Pam is realizing that even if she did pass the course, this isn't for her.
帕姆意识到，就算她通过了这门课程，这也不适合她。

1664
01:08:08.620 --> 01:08:10.880
But she's also embarrassed that she failed.
但她也为自己挂科感到难堪。

1665
01:08:11.600 --> 01:08:18.240
But what she definitely does not want to do is spend 12 more weeks studying something she doesn't love.
但她绝对不想再花12周去学习一件她并不热爱的事情。

1666
01:08:18.600 --> 01:08:22.780
For me, in that moment, I just saw Pam stating her truth.
对我来说，那一刻我只看到帕姆在陈述她的真心话。

1667
01:08:23.000 --> 01:08:25.200
And I always think that's so powerful.
我一直觉得那非常有力量。

1668
01:08:25.680 --> 01:08:25.860
Yeah.
是啊。

1669
01:08:26.100 --> 01:08:30.580
There is a very sweet deleted scene, you guys, with Jim and Pam.
伙计们，有一个关于吉姆和帕姆的删减片段非常温馨。

1670
01:08:30.780 --> 01:08:32.080
It's in the break room.
是在休息室里发生的。

1671
01:08:32.260 --> 01:08:33.220
And you know what?
你知道吗？

1672
01:08:33.360 --> 01:08:34.260
I'm titling it.
我给它起了个标题。

1673
01:08:34.520 --> 01:08:34.960
What?
什么？

1674
01:08:35.200 --> 01:08:36.440
Love in the break room.
休息室里的爱。

1675
01:08:36.660 --> 01:08:37.640
What is it?
那是什么？

1676
01:08:38.180 --> 01:08:40.620
Pam is showing Jim her art assignment.
帕姆在给吉姆看她的艺术作业。

1677
01:08:40.880 --> 01:08:41.880
She has this portfolio.
她有一个作品集。

1678
01:08:42.120 --> 01:08:45.680
And she's showing him the piece that she got an F on.
她正在给他看那个得了F的作品。

1679
01:08:45.960 --> 01:08:48.360
Oh, I remember shooting this now.
哦，我现在记起拍这场戏了。

1680
01:08:48.480 --> 01:08:49.040
Yes.
是的。

1681
01:08:49.180 --> 01:08:49.440
Yes.
没错。

1682
01:08:49.680 --> 01:08:51.340
Oh, I remember it.
哦，我记得。

1683
01:08:51.420 --> 01:08:52.580
It's really sweet.
真的很温馨。

1684
01:08:52.820 --> 01:08:58.960
And as he goes through her art assignments, in the back, tucked in the binder, is a sketch pad.
当他翻看她的艺术作业时，在活页夹的后面夹着一本素描本。

1685
01:08:59.640 --> 01:09:01.000
And he's like, what is this?
他问，这是什么？

1686
01:09:01.100 --> 01:09:04.920
And she said, oh, you know, it's just sketches of things I would see in New York.
她说，哦，你知道的，那只是我在纽约看到的一些事物的素描。

1687
01:09:05.740 --> 01:09:12.240
And when you look at them, Jenna, and I'll put it in stories, it's like people sitting at a cafe, things she might have seen on her walk.
当你看到它们的时候，珍娜——我会把它发到快拍里——就像是人们坐在咖啡馆里，或者她在散步时可能看到的东西。

1688
01:09:12.240 --> 01:09:13.840
And they're really good.
而且它们真的画得很好。

1689
01:09:14.180 --> 01:09:16.220
And this is such a wonderful moment.
这是一个非常美妙的时刻。

1690
01:09:16.420 --> 01:09:17.780
I wish it had stayed in.
真希望它能保留下来。

1691
01:09:18.160 --> 01:09:19.360
Sam, can you play the clip?
萨姆，能播放一下片段吗？

1692
01:09:20.280 --> 01:09:21.280
This is my project.
这是我的作业。

1693
01:09:22.380 --> 01:09:24.220
Before we start, how did you fail?
在我们开始之前，你是怎么挂科的？

1694
01:09:24.760 --> 01:09:25.820
You're good at art.
你很擅长艺术啊。

1695
01:09:26.960 --> 01:09:27.360
See?
你看？

1696
01:09:27.840 --> 01:09:28.240
Yeah.
是啊。

1697
01:09:28.500 --> 01:09:30.280
We had to make a logo for a coffee company.
我们得为一家咖啡公司设计一个标志。

1698
01:09:30.420 --> 01:09:30.840
Well, that's nice.
嗯，那个挺不错的。

1699
01:09:31.060 --> 01:09:32.020
This is the one that got an A.
这是那个得了A的作品。

1700
01:09:32.140 --> 01:09:33.120
The teacher handed it out.
老师把它发下来了。

1701
01:09:33.160 --> 01:09:33.440
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1702
01:09:33.440 --> 01:09:34.700
And this is mine.
这是我的。

1703
01:09:35.160 --> 01:09:35.680
Well, that's cool.
嗯，那挺酷的。

1704
01:09:35.960 --> 01:09:38.020
I couldn't get it to print out right, so I got an F.
我没法把它打印出来，所以得了个F。

1705
01:09:38.460 --> 01:09:39.380
I would have given you a D.
我本来会给你个D的。

1706
01:09:39.980 --> 01:09:41.700
That's only because we were sleeping with a professor.
那只是因为我们当时和教授睡过。

1707
01:09:43.000 --> 01:09:43.760
These are cool.
这些很酷。

1708
01:09:45.300 --> 01:09:45.920
What's this?
这是什么？

1709
01:09:46.540 --> 01:09:47.600
That's my sketchbook.
那是我的素描本。

1710
01:09:48.060 --> 01:09:50.080
It's just, you know, stuff I saw in New York.
就是，你知道，我在纽约看到的一些东西。

1711
01:09:50.260 --> 01:09:50.960
People on the subway.
地铁上的人们。

1712
01:09:51.600 --> 01:09:52.040
Whoa.
哇。

1713
01:09:52.960 --> 01:09:54.280
This is great.
这太棒了。

1714
01:09:54.660 --> 01:09:56.600
It's so much different than your other work.
这和你之前的作品很不一样。

1715
01:09:57.380 --> 01:09:58.380
Wow, Pam.
哇，帕姆。

1716
01:09:59.320 --> 01:10:00.600
That is awesome.
那真是太厉害了。

1717
01:10:01.380 --> 01:10:01.820
Yeah?
是吗？

1718
01:10:03.840 --> 01:10:04.420
Yeah.
是啊。

1719
01:10:05.720 --> 01:10:07.420
Oh, I wish that had stayed in.
噢，我真希望那段没被剪掉。

1720
01:10:07.600 --> 01:10:14.500
It's a really sweet scene, and I feel like it just shows what Pam did get out of New York,
那是一个非常温馨的场景，我觉得它正好展现了帕姆在纽约的收获，

1721
01:10:14.500 --> 01:10:16.680
and I really wish it had been in the episode.
我真的很希望它能出现在那一集里。

1722
01:10:16.880 --> 01:10:21.540
I agree, because I don't think Pam's art story is over yet.
我同意，因为我觉得帕姆的艺术之路还没结束。

1723
01:10:21.740 --> 01:10:22.100
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1724
01:10:22.580 --> 01:10:30.540
You know, she did not have the benefit of, I think, parents or role models who encouraged
你知道，她没有那种父母或榜样来鼓励她，

1725
01:10:30.540 --> 01:10:37.780
encouraged her to follow this piece of herself, and she only finally does now have that person
鼓励她去追随这部分的自我，而她现在终于有了那个人，

1726
01:10:37.780 --> 01:10:38.340
in gym.
就是吉姆。

1727
01:10:38.500 --> 01:10:38.860
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1728
01:10:39.020 --> 01:10:44.160
So she's going to have to take her art journey at the same time as her romantic journey.
所以她必须在开启浪漫旅程的同时，也开启她的艺术之旅。

1729
01:10:44.660 --> 01:10:47.860
Well, I'm going to put that scene in stories, because it's really sweet.
好吧，我会把那个场景放进故事里，因为它真的很温馨。

1730
01:10:47.860 --> 01:10:49.020
I loved it.
我很喜欢。

1731
01:10:49.120 --> 01:10:49.760
I did, too.
我也是。

1732
01:10:50.200 --> 01:10:52.220
Well, that kind of wraps up this episode.
好了，这一集就到这里。

1733
01:10:52.620 --> 01:10:52.840
Yeah.
是啊。

1734
01:10:53.180 --> 01:10:56.100
Thank you to everyone who helped us make this episode.
感谢所有帮助我们制作这一集的人。

1735
01:10:56.180 --> 01:10:56.500
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1736
01:10:56.660 --> 01:11:03.140
Brent Forrester, Randy Cordray, Wendy McClendon-Covey, and Rich Sommer, thanks for coming on for an
布伦特·福雷斯特、兰迪·科德雷、温迪·麦克伦登-科薇和里奇·索莫，感谢你们来接受

1737
01:11:03.140 --> 01:11:03.560
interview.
采访。

1738
01:11:03.880 --> 01:11:05.060
It takes a village.
众人拾柴火焰高。

1739
01:11:05.220 --> 01:11:05.660
It does.
确实。

1740
01:11:05.660 --> 01:11:10.040
And thank you to you guys for sending in awesome questions and Winnipeg trivia.
也感谢你们大家发来很棒的问题和关于温尼伯的冷知识。

1741
01:11:10.380 --> 01:11:10.820
Yes.
是的。

1742
01:11:11.120 --> 01:11:12.840
Some last parting advice.
最后给大家一点建议。

1743
01:11:13.280 --> 01:11:19.640
According to Andy, Long Island iced teas are way stronger in Canada, so be careful the next
据安迪说，长岛冰茶在加拿大的后劲大得多，所以下次点的时候要小心。

1744
01:11:19.640 --> 01:11:20.860
time you order one of those.
点的时候要小心。

1745
01:11:21.240 --> 01:11:21.740
Yes.
是的。

1746
01:11:22.340 --> 01:11:23.480
All right, you guys.
好了，各位。

1747
01:11:23.700 --> 01:11:27.260
Well, that was Business Trip, and we will be seeing you next week.
那么，这就是《出差》这一集，我们下周见。

1748
01:11:27.460 --> 01:11:28.780
Yeah, see you next week.
好的，下周见。

1749
01:11:32.130 --> 01:11:34.090
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

